Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.23.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.23.0 rebuilds the shell Stheno-style and fixes the broken corner resize. Resize root cause (log-evidenced): after hosting/recovery the keepalive geometry-hold kept writing win/scene geometry back to the old size three times within one second, so any user resize was snapped back - now a user-gesture gate suspends all geometry corrections (content-view fix and scene.frame correct) during the resize gesture and for 1.5 s after it ends; resize now also logs begin/end so the next log proves whether the recognizer fired; the grip hit area grows from 24 to 44 pt. Chrome removal: the window body is fully transparent with no border, title/status text hidden, top/bottom bars become invisible edge strips (still move handles), content area fills the whole window, and the corner grip shows a faint arrow. App picking is now gesture-driven: double-tap (default) or long-press on the edge strips toggles the app-picker overlay with the hosted view, configured by the new pickerGesture key (0=off 1=double-tap 2=long-press). A new defaultBundleID key auto-hosts the given app 0.6 s after the window appears when non-empty (default-open). cfgVersion migrates 19 to 20 for these two keys; hosting, snapshot anti-flash and daemon recovery logic are otherwise unchanged.
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
